  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "9de44423394498f5bd6649fb4ff9fb4b7226fbd6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1883225324,
          "type": null,
          "body": "This won't really have any effect, so I don't believe it's responsible for your issue.\n\nThe only difference between `wslua_checkint32(L,1)` and `wslua_checkuint32(L,1)` is that the former casts the result to a `int32_t` and the latter to a `uint32_t`, but since `proto_tree_add_int` casts the last parameter to a `int32_t` the end result is the same. (With fixed width integer types.)\n\nIt doesn't hurt, but it's not causing your problem.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-26T20:44:12.127Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-26T20:44:12.127Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 298637161,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 15438,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0090eb61a15ce1022e97d38299e0f6423b7e2ab5",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1883234569,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> This won't really have any effect, so I don't believe it's responsible for your issue.\n\nI thought that too, and then I tried it! Turns out on a Mac, casting from a floating point to an unsigned integer *does* take the nearest value (i.e. 0) instead of the unsigned interpretation of the nearest signed integer value!\n\nhttps://github.com/mavlink/mavlink/issues/2073#issuecomment-2080103820\n\n> > I guess that somewhere in this lot, the behaviour between Mac and Linux differs, and the negative number gets cut at 0.\n> > Maybe the equivalent of something like this (which prints -100 on Linux):\n> > ```c\n> >   double x = -100;\n> >   unsigned int y = (unsigned int)x;\n> > ```\n> \n> Honestly, I thought that was a ridiculous suggestion and there's no way that differs between Linux and Mac. ...but it turns out you're right! It does indeed print 0 on my computer when compiling with both clang 15 and gcc 13!",
          "author": {
            "id": 292560,
            "username": "rotu",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dan Rose",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/817768956c9b0bb4b029a8ac0d3d4edeb599a858acd5a78168c21f479568aacf?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rotu"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-04-26T20:55:05.751Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-04-26T20:55:05.751Z",
