    {
      "id": "8a586d366defaf1175cf2a857c7d12072b1142c5",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1883461232,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Also, we may want, at least on the current master branch, to change those functions to use `checkinteger` now that we are moving to Lua 5.3 and Lua 5.4.\n\nPlease clarify. Despite the name, the macros *are* using `luaL_checkinteger` and not `luaL_checkint`.\n\nAt any rate, to make any such change, I think I must first understand why `wslua_checkint` and `wslua_checkint32` use different conversion functions to start with (`luaL_checkinteger` vs `luaL_checknumber`). Any insights?\n\n```c\n#define wslua_checkint(L,i)    (int)             ( luaL_checkinteger(L,i) )\n#define wslua_checkint32(L,i)  (int32_t)         ( luaL_checknumber(L,i) )\n#define wslua_checkint64(L,i)  (int64_t)         ( luaL_checknumber(L,i) )\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 292560,
            "username": "rotu",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Dan Rose",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/817768956c9b0bb4b029a8ac0d3d4edeb599a858acd5a78168c21f479568aacf?s=80&d=identicon",
