        {
          "id": 1883705088,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "`luaL_checkint` does not exist in Lua 5.3 and later. Sometimes things are removed but exist in compatibility mode for another major version.\n\nLua 5.2 and earlier use a single Number type which is usually a double (it doesn't have to be; it can even be an integer type in which case the language as installed doesn't support floating point). When Lua 5.2 and earlier use `luaL_checkinteger(L,i)` they still end up storing the value as a double, but pass through some checks and casts. When casting the `Lua_Integer` type is a `ptrdiff_t`, which is 32 bit on 32 bit machines.\n\nFor that reason, the sized checkint functions use `luaL_checknumber(L,i)` and then cast, because `luaL_checkinteger(L,i)` cannot handle 64 bit integers on a 32 bit machine properly. It also doesn't handle anything in the upper half of a 32 bit signed integer on a 32 bit machine nor anything in the upper half of a 64 bit integer on a 64 bit machine. There's a specific function to convert known unsigned integers to doubles, but it was changed in Lua 5.3 to give incorrect results and is deprecated.\n\nIn Lua 5.3 and later numbers are a union stored as a Number type (usually a double) and an Integer type (usually whatever type, including `long long`, is necessary to be 64 bits, always signed.) That is usually 64 bit on any platform (32 bit or 64 bit platform), but the language can be configured at its compile time to be only 32 bit on any platform.\n\nOn Lua 5.3 and later, the `luaL_checkinteger(L,i)` function results in storing the number in the Integer part of the union. This always stores it as a signed integer, and there's no way (not with `pushunsigned` either) to record that the number was unsigned originally; you have to know when accessing it and cast. (Which, by default, only affects the top half of the 64 bit unsigned integer range.)\n\nWireshark has UserTypes that implement signed and unsigned 64 bit integers for this reason.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
